(Track B3 fallback: /dev/null is a character device, not a regular file, so
 _read_into_buffer must skip pre-sizing and fall back to the doubling loop.
 Reading it yields zero bytes immediately; the buffer stays empty and intact,
 capacity is unchanged, and there is no crash.)

a buffer called dyn is "".
open a file for reading called nf at "/dev/null".
Read from nf into dyn.
Close nf.

Print "length:".
Print dyn's size.
Print "capacity:".
Print dyn's capacity.